"Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree costs $90 to plant. Each year it grows 7 lemons, selling for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the lemon tree?","Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree will cost $90 to plant. Each year it will grow 7 lemons, which he can sell for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the lemon tree?",13,13,13,13,"Carlos needs to recover the initial $90 cost and annual net profits. Each year, the tree generates $10.5 from selling lemons (7 lemons * $1.5 each) and incurs $3 in costs, resulting in a net annual profit of $7.5. The total profit after n years is $7.5n. To cover the initial $90, solve $7.5n ≥ 90. Dividing 90 by 7.5 gives n = 12. However, at n = 12, the profit exactly equals the initial cost (break-even). Earning money starts when profit exceeds the initial cost, which occurs in the 13th year.

