"To be promoted, Jane takes 3 tests totaling at least 42 points. On her first test, she scored 15 points, on the second 18 points. What is the minimum she must score on the third test to pass?","To be promoted to the next school year, Jane takes 3 tests that together must total at least 42 points. On her first test, Jane scored 15 points, on the second test she scored 18 points. What is the minimum number of points she must score on the third test to pass?",9,9,9,9,"To determine the minimum score Jane needs on her third test, first calculate the total points she has from the first two tests:  
15 (first test) + 18 (second test) = 33 points.  

