But then, unexpectedly, 40 guests showed up. So the actual number of guests is 40, not 36. Now, everyone wanted a second hotdog. So each of the 40 guests wants two hotdogs. That means the total needed would be 40 * 2 = 80 hotdogs. But the caterer only had 54 available. So the difference is 80 - 54 = 26 hotdogs short. But the question is how many guests did not get a second hotdog?

