But wait, the problem says, ""everyone wanted a second hotdog"". So the caterer needs to provide 2 per person. But he prepared 54. Let me verify again to make sure.

Original preparation:

He was told 36 guests. He prepared for half of them (18) to have two, and the rest (18) one each. So total hotdogs = (18*2) + (18*1) = 36 +18 =54.

But when 40 guests came, all wanting two, he serves each guest one first. So 40 hotdogs. Then, he has 54-40=14 left for seconds. So, of the 40 guests, 14 can get a second. That leaves 40-14=26 guests who didn't get their second hotdog.

