So, she has six decks of basketball cards, each with 25. So 6 decks × 25 cards per deck. Let me do that: 6 × 25. Hmm, 25 times 6, that's 150. So 150 basketball cards.

Then, five boxes of baseball cards, each with 40. So 5 × 40. That's 200. So 200 baseball cards.

Total cards altogether would be 150 + 200. Let me add those. 150 plus 200 is 350 cards in total.

Now, she keeps 50. So subtract that from the total. 350 - 50 = 300. So there are 300 cards left to give to students.

Each student gets 10 cards, so I divide 300 by 10. 300 ÷ 10 equals 30. So there are 30 students.

