"There are 30 students in Marissa’s class, which is located on the second floor of the school building. Each student started the year with 10 pencils. After two months, 1/5 of the total pencils in class were used. At the end of the year, only 1/3 of the remaining pencils were left. How many pencils were left?","There are 30 students in Marissa’s class. Each student started the year with 10 pencils. After two months, 1/5 of the total pencils in class were used. At the end of the year, only 1/3 of the remaining pencils were left. How many pencils were left?",80,80,80,80,"The class starts with 30 students × 10 pencils each = 300 pencils.  
After two months, 1/5 of 300 pencils are used: 300 × (1/5) = 60 used. Remaining: 300 - 60 = 240.  
At the end of the year, 1/3 of the remaining 240 pencils are left: 240 × (1/3) = 80.  
