The school auditorium has 4 rows of seats. There are 18 seats in each row. One-fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators. One-third of the remaining seats were occupied by parents and the rest by students. How many students were there in the school auditorium?,The school auditorium has 4 rows of seats. There are 18 seats in each row. One-fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators. One-third of the remaining seats were occupied by the parents and the rest were occupied by the students. How many students were there in the school auditorium?,36,36,36,36,"The school auditorium has 4 rows with 18 seats each, totaling 4 × 18 = 72 seats. Administrators occupy one-fourth of the seats: 72 × (1/4) = 18 seats. The remaining seats are 72 - 18 = 54. Parents occupy one-third of the remaining seats: 54 × (1/3) = 18 seats. The rest of the seats are occupied by students: 54 - 18 = 36 seats.

