Brenda invested $300 into a scheme that accumulates simple interest at three-quarters of the original amount per year. How much in total will she have after 3 years?,Brenda invested $300 into a scheme that accumulates simple interest at the rate of three-quarters of the original amount per year. How much in total will she have after 3 years?,975,975,975,975,"Brenda's principal amount is $300. The simple interest earned each year is three-quarters of the original amount, which is (3/4) * $300 = $225 per year. Over 3 years, the total interest accumulated is $225/year * 3 years = $675. Adding this to the principal, the total amount after 3 years is $300 + $675 = $975.

