Half of them have collars, so half of 40 is 20. Therefore, white shirts with collars: 20. That leaves the white shirts without collars as 40 - 20 = 20. Wait, wait, if half have collars, the other half would also be 20. Yeah, that makes sense. So white shirts without collars are 20.

Now, floral shirts: 50 total. 20 of them have buttons. So the ones without buttons would be 50 - 20 = 30. So floral shirts without buttons: 30.

The question is asking how many more floral shirts without buttons than white shirts without collars. So I subtract the number of white shirts without collars from floral shirts without buttons. So 30 (floral no buttons) minus 20 (white no collars) = 10. So the answer should be 10. Let me just check each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.

Wait, the problem says half of the white shirts have collars, so that's 40 divided by 2, which is 20. So yes, 20 white shirts with collars and 20 without. Then floral shirts total 50. 20 have buttons, so 50 -20 is 30. That math checks out. So then 30 - 20 =10. Seems right.
