"John rents his car out 10 times a month for 3 hours each. He gets $25 an hour. If his car payment is $500, how much profit does he make?","John rents his car out 10 times a month for 3 hours each time. He gets paid $25 an hour. If his car payment is $500, how much profit does he make on his car?",250,250,250,250,"John rents his car 10 times a month for 3 hours each, totaling 10 × 3 = 30 hours. At $25 per hour, his earnings are 30 × $25 = $750. Subtracting the $500 car payment, his profit is $750 - $500 = $250.

#### 250","Okay, let me try to figure out this problem step by step. So, John rents out his car 10 times a month, each time for 3 hours. He gets $25 per hour. We need to find out his profit after paying his car payment of $500.

