Then the big coupons: 1400 coupons times 15 cents each. That might be a bit trickier. Let me calculate that. Maybe break it down into easier parts. 1400 × 15. Well, 15 is 10 + 5. So 1400×10 is 14,000 cents, and 1400×5 is 7,000 cents. Then adding those together: 14,000 +7,000 = 21,000 cents. So the big coupons cost 21,000 cents.

